                                "sense_id": "b21fb074-0df6-3ca3-bb79-1332867bb9aa",
                                "text": "Many epiphytic plants solve this problem by forming symbiotic relationships with ants, that is, relationships that involve the close and long-term living together of two species. The plants provide their insect partners with shelter and a supply of nectar, while the ants return the favor by serving as a source of fertilizer – in the form of fecal matter."
